C++ character array. Pretty neat, and it only took 8 SLOC in <code class=3D=
"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">CMakeRC.cmake</code>!</p>

<p>There=E2=80=99s a problem, though: We=E2=80=99ve named the two pointers =
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">file_begin</code> and
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">file_end</code>, and w=
e never vary them when compiling files. This means that we can
only compile one resource into our binary, ever! That=E2=80=99s pretty usel=
ess=E2=80=A6</p>

<p>In addition, how do we go about accessing the contents from <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cmrc::open</code>? We
could just return a pointer to <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighte=
r-rouge">file_begin</code> and <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighte=
r-rouge">file_end</code>, but we want to get
rid of names those and somehow access based on filename. Hm=E2=80=A6</p>

<h2 id=3D"step-4-encoding-the-filesystem-structure">Step 4: Encoding the Fi=
lesystem Structure</h2>

<p>We want to be able to access things by the path from which they were com=
piled,
so we must somehow encode the file paths into both the symbol names as well=
 as
some kind of lookup-table that is searched at runtime based on filenames.</=
p>

<h3 id=3D"step-4a-generating-identifierssymbols">Step 4a: Generating Identi=
fiers/Symbols</h3>

<p>This is actually a fairly simple task. We want to make a symbol based on=
 the
name of the file that is passed in to <code class=3D"language-plaintext hig=
hlighter-rouge">cmrc_add_resource_library</code>. Let=E2=80=99s make
a function to do that:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">function</span><span class=
=3D"p">(</span>_cm_encode_fpath var fpath<span class=3D"p">)</span>
    <span class=3D"nb">string</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>MAKE_C_IDENTI=
FIER <span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"=
nv">fpath</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> iden=
t<span class=3D"p">)</span>
    <span class=3D"nb">string</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>MD5 hash <spa=
n class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">fpath=
</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D=
"p">)</span>
    <span class=3D"nb">string</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>SUBSTRING <sp=
an class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">hash=
</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> 0 4 hash<span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>
