<p>It=E2=80=99s fairly simple as well: It reads in the path to the source i=
mage as a
command line argument, checks that the size of the file on disk and file in
memory are the same, then checks that they are byte-for-byte identical. Her=
e=E2=80=99s
the definition for this executable and test case in the <code class=3D"lang=
uage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">CMakeLists.txt</code>:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">add_executable</span><span =
class=3D"p">(</span>flower flower.cpp<span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">target_link_libraries</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>fl=
ower PRIVATE hello<span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">add_test</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>flower flower <=
span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR</spa=
n><span class=3D"si">}</span>/flower.jpg<span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>We just need to add a <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-roug=
e">flower.jpg</code> file into the source directory. The
particular image is unimportant, but I=E2=80=99ve chosen a 2.5 MB image fro=
m WikiMedia
Commons in the public domain, <a href=3D"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikip=
edia/commons/0/0c/White_and_yellow_flower.JPG">found here</a>.</p>

<p>Running CTest again, the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-r=
ouge">flower</code> test will fail because the resource size is
zero! That=E2=80=99s because we haven=E2=80=99t added it to the <code class=
=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">hello</code> resource library.</p=
>

