few things have happened.</p>

<h3 id=3D"fix-dependency-ordering">Fix Dependency Ordering</h3>

<p>While it didn=E2=80=99t break anything, we had a bit of sadness in the w=
ay CMake
evaluated our dependencies. The trouble was that every time the user ran th=
e
CMake configure, we=E2=80=99d re-write the <code class=3D"language-plaintex=
t highlighter-rouge">cmrc.hpp</code> and <code class=3D"language-plaintext =
highlighter-rouge">lib.cpp</code> files. Build tools
that work on timestamps (most of them) would consider every file that inclu=
ded
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cmrc.hpp</code> to be =
out-of-date and would rebuild them, <em>even if the file had
identical contents</em>. No good.</p>

<p>To fix the issue with <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-roug=
e">cmrc.hpp</code>, we split generating the file into a phase
where we generate the string content, then write the file <em>only</em> if =
the content
on disk has changed. That means this:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">file</span><span class=3D"p=
">(</span>WRITE <span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><spa=
n class=3D"nv">CMRC_INCLUDE_DIR</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span clas=
s=3D"s2">/cmrc/cmrc.hpp"</span> <span class=3D"s2">[[&lt;content&gt;]]</spa=
n><span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>becomes this:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">set</span><span class=3D"p"=
>(</span>hpp_content <span class=3D"s2">[[&lt;content&gt;]]</span><span cla=
ss=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">set</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>cmrc_hpp <span class=
=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">CMRC_INCLUDE=
_DIR</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">/cmrc/cmrc.hpp"</s=
pan> CACHE INTERNAL <span class=3D"s2">""</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">set</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>_generate 1<span cla=
ss=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">if</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>EXISTS <span class=3D=
"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">cmrc_hpp</span>=
<span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"p">)</=
span>
    <span class=3D"nb">file</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>READ <span clas=
s=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">cmrc_hpp</s=
pan><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> _current<span cl=
ass=3D"p">)</span>
    <span class=3D"nb">if</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>_current STREQUAL=
 hpp_content<span class=3D"p">)</span>
        <span class=3D"nb">set</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>_generate 0<=
span class=3D"p">)</span>
    <span class=3D"nb">endif</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
<span class=3D"nb">endif</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
<span class=3D"nb">file</span><span class=3D"p">(</span>GENERATE OUTPUT <sp=
an class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">cmrc=
_hpp</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> CONTENT <=
span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">hp=
p_content</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> COND=
ITION <span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">_generate</span><span =
class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>In the above, we set <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge=
">hpp_content</code> to the file contents, then read the
already-existing file (if it exists). We set a <code class=3D"language-plai=
ntext highlighter-rouge">_generate</code> variable to <code class=3D"langua=
ge-plaintext highlighter-rouge">1</code> if
we need to generate, otherwise <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighte=
r-rouge">0</code>. The <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"=
>file(GENERATE ...)</code> line will
conditionally write the file depending on the value of <code class=3D"langu=
age-plaintext highlighter-rouge">_generate</code>.</p>

<p>Generating the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">lib.=
cpp</code> file is a little more complex because we don=E2=80=99t know
what it=E2=80=99s final content will be at the time we call <code class=3D"=
language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">file(GENERATE ...)</code> for
it. For this reason, we instead use <code class=3D"language-plaintext highl=
