<h3 id=3D"fix-the-libdir-path-bug">Fix the <code class=3D"language-plaintex=
t highlighter-rouge">libdir</code> Path Bug</h3>

<p><code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cmrc_add_resources<=
/code> had a bug: It used the <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter=
-rouge">libdir</code> variable that was set locally in the <code class=3D"l=
anguage-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cmrc_add_resource_library</code> funct=
ion. This variable told it where to put generated files for the resource li=
brary. If this variable wasn=E2=80=99t set, <code class=3D"language-plainte=
xt highlighter-rouge">cmrc_add_resources</code> added files at incorrect pa=
ths.</p>

<p>Since <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">libdir</code>=
 is associated with the resource library, we=E2=80=99ll set it as a target
property in <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">cmrc_add_r=
esource_library</code>:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">set_property</span><span cl=
ass=3D"p">(</span>TARGET <span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">nam=
e</span><span class=3D"si">}</span> PROPERTY CMRC_LIBDIR <span class=3D"s2"=
>"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">libdir</span><span =
class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>And read it back in <code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"=
>cmrc_add_resources</code>:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">get_target_property</span><=
span class=3D"p">(</span>libdir <span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"=
nv">name</span><span class=3D"si">}</span> CMRC_LIBDIR<span class=3D"p">)</=
span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<h3 id=3D"generate-the-intermediate-c-files-faster">Generate the Intermedia=
te C++ Files Faster</h3>

<p>For large input files, generating the C++ code takes a while. On my mach=
ine,
encoding a 10MB file of random bytes takes about 22 seconds. It=E2=80=99s n=
ot
<em>horrible</em>, but it could be faster.</p>

<p>For this speedup, I changed the generated code a bit: Instead of writing=
 a
literal array of characters, I generate a single string literal of <code cl=
ass=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">\xNN</code>
escapes. No need to worry about commas.</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>I also tried to generate a single big C++11 raw-string literal of the =
raw
input content, but certain sequence of bytes simply won=E2=80=99t be accept=
ed by the
compiler.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>The biggest speedup I could manage was by doing the transform with more =
than
one byte at a time. Experimentation reveals that doing <em>five</em> bytes =
per regex
match gives the best performance. That means that this:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">string</span><span class=3D=
"p">(</span>REGEX REPLACE <span class=3D"s2">"(..)"</span> <span class=3D"s=
2">"'</span><span class=3D"se">\\\\</span><span class=3D"s2">x</span><span =
class=3D"se">\\</span><span class=3D"s2">1', "</span> chars <span class=3D"=
s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">bytes</span><spa=
n class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"p">)</span=
>
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>becomes this:</p>

<div class=3D"language-cmake highlighter-rouge"><div class=3D"highlight"><p=
re class=3D"highlight"><code><span class=3D"nb">string</span><span class=3D=
"p">(</span>REGEX REPLACE <span class=3D"s2">"(..)(..)(..)(..)(..)"</span> =
<span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"se">\\\\</span><span class=3D"s2"=
>x</span><span class=3D"se">\\</span><span class=3D"s2">1</span><span class=
=3D"se">\\\\</span><span class=3D"s2">x</span><span class=3D"se">\\</span><=
span class=3D"s2">2</span><span class=3D"se">\\\\</span><span class=3D"s2">=
x</span><span class=3D"se">\\</span><span class=3D"s2">3</span><span class=
