nup_sub</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span> chars =
<span class=3D"s2">"</span><span class=3D"si">${</span><span class=3D"nv">c=
hars</span><span class=3D"si">}</span><span class=3D"s2">"</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"nb">endif</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</code></pre></div></div>

<blockquote>
  <p>Doing math in CMake code is a miserable experience.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>We=E2=80=99ll also need to fix the pointer to the resource end. Since we=
 are using a
string literal character array, we=E2=80=99ll have an extra null terminator=
 that wasn=E2=80=99t
in the original file. Instead of using <code class=3D"language-plaintext hi=
ghlighter-rouge">sizeof(file_array)</code>, well just drop
<code class=3D"language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">@n_bytes@</code> into =
the code template. This has the edded benefit that we can now
guarantee that resource file pointers are null-terminated.</p>

<p>With this change, processing a 10MB file only takes ten seconds on my ma=
chine.
It=E2=80=99s still <em>way</em> slower than if we did this in native code, =
but the speed issue
isn=E2=80=99t a huge concern since we can process multiple files in paralle=
l and
resources are rarely more than several megabytes.</p>

<p>Again, all the code can be found and downloaded <a href=3D"https://githu=
b.com/vector-of-bool/cmrc">on GitHub</a>.</p>

